    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b59c6ae3-b0c9-51c8-9fe5-f6714e9067eb",
      ":question/problem": "What is $\\int 6^{4 x - 5}\\,\\text{d}x$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "If we let $u=4 x - 5,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6^{4 x - 5}\\,\\text{d}x&=\\int 6^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{4}\\int 6^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{4}\\frac{6^{u}}{\\ln 6}+C \\\\ &=\\frac{6^{4 x - 5}}{4 \\ln{\\left(6 \\right)}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
